# Ubuntu Client display selection

Branch: client-displays, based on main and the complete 1.2.02 Client.
Scope: Ubuntu Qt Client. Host protocol and macOS Client behavior stay unchanged.

## Behavior

- Add per-bookmark Client Displays: current monitor, a named connected monitor,
  or both side-by-side monitors. New bookmarks use current; saved bookmarks
  without the new key retain their existing spanning behavior.
- Resolve connector identities on the GUI thread before authentication. Use
  that same selection for Mac display preparation, Linux Match Client geometry
  and the initial Qt presentation. Do not persist transient enumeration indices.
- Keep Host layout and scaling independent. At 100% scale, a matching single
  stream fills its selected fullscreen display with no window decorations.
- Add a small menu beside the existing fullscreen control: fullscreen on this
  monitor or span both. These are local, session-only presentation changes;
  they do not change the negotiated Host layout, stream or bookmark.
- Keep the selected monitor when moving between windowed and fullscreen states.
  Missing saved monitors fall back to the current monitor with visible feedback.
- Release held input on focus/layout changes. Permit the pointer to cross between
  independent fullscreen sessions; background sessions must not receive pen input.

## Validation

- Test selection persistence, absent monitors, stable selection after enumeration
  changes, equal/unequal displays, and 100%/125% physical versus logical geometry.
- Test single-monitor Match Client for Linux and Mac preparation, and ensure
  session presentation overrides do not mutate the negotiated display snapshot.
- Exercise two independent fullscreen windows and single/span/windowed transitions
  in the existing isolated GNOME compositor, including popup input isolation.
- Run the complete Ubuntu hosted build, sanitizer, compositor and package gates;
  collect the branch-labelled candidate with its original manifest and hashes.
- User hardware acceptance: two different Hosts fullscreen one per monitor,
  exact pixel fit, toolbar, focus/keyboard/Wacom, span and reconnect. Hosted
  software-GPU results do not replace this acceptance.

The deferred Intel GPU-hang/packet-loss investigation remains paused.

## Candidate validation

Version 1.2.04-client-displays passed hosted build41116553672, including normal
and sanitized selection/QML/input tests, both compositor scales, simultaneous
fullscreen windows on two outputs, precision and package checks. The toolbar
menu screenshot was inspected after correcting its initial text truncation.
See HANDOFF for exact source/package hashes. Live two-session hardware and
keyboard/tablet focus acceptance remain pending; no deployment or merge yet.
